# Git Workflow

- **After making any code or config changes** in this project, run `git add -A` so all changes are staged. The user will commit via Cursor's Source Control UI.
- **Do not run `git commit` or `git push`** unless the user explicitly asks you to (e.g. "commit and push", "push to git", "commit these changes").
- When the user says they will "commit via Cursor" or "commit myself", only stage changes with `git add -A`; never run commit or push.
